  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Virendra vs State Of U.P. on 7 July, 2020 Author: Siddharth Bench: Siddharth High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Court No. - 82 Case :- Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. - 18328 of 2020 Applicant :- Virendra Opposite Party :- State of U.P. Counsel for Applicant :- Rajesh Kumar Srivastava,Gaurav Kumar Srivastava,Virendra Kumar Counsel for Opposite Party :- G.A. Hon'ble Siddharth,J. Order on the Exemption Application Application is allowed.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "learned counsel for the applicant and learned A.G.A. Submission is that Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 has been enacted by the legislature and hence the implication of the applicant under section 272, 273 I.P.C. is unjustified. Offence under section 60(1) of Excise Act is bailable and triable by Magistrate. False recovery has been alleged. The applicant is languishing in jail since 29.3.2020, who is not a previous convict. Learned A.G.A. has opposed the bail prayer of the applicant. Keeping in view the nature of the offence, argument advanced on behalf of the parties, evidence on record regarding complicity of the accused, larger mandate of the Article 21 of the Constitution of Virendra vs State Of U.P. on 7 July, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/171571065/ 1 India and the dictum of Apex Court in the case of Dataram Singh Vs. State of U.P. and another reported in (2018)3 SCC 22",
    "petitioner_arguments": "learned counsel for the applicant and learned A.G.A. Submission is that Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 has been enacted by the legislature and hence the implication of the applicant under section 272, 273 I.P.C. is unjustified. Offence under section 60(1) of Excise Act is bailable and triable by Magistrate. False recovery has been alleged. The applicant is languishing in jail since 29.3.2020, who is not a previous convict. Learned A.G.A. has opposed the bail prayer of the applicant.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Keeping in view the nature of the offence, argument advanced on behalf of the parties, evidence on record regarding complicity of the accused, larger mandate of the Article 21 of the Constitution of Virendra vs State Of U.P. on 7 July, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/171571065/ 1 India and the dictum of Apex Court in the case of Dataram Singh Vs. State of U.P. and another reported in (2018)3 SCC 22"
  },
